# Introduction

This project focuses on implementing and analyzing regularized regression techniques, with a specific emphasis on LASSO and Ridge regression. In Task 1, we develop a custom implementation of the LASSO algorithm using the shooting method, evaluate it over a range of penalty parameters (λ), and compare its performance against the glmnet package. We also implement 10-fold cross-validation to select the optimal λ and validate the results using simulated data.

In Task 2, we apply these techniques to the Hitters dataset from the ISLR package, using the Salary variable as the response. The dataset is split into training and testing sets, and the optimal λ for LASSO is determined. Ridge regression and ordinary least squares (OLS) models are also fitted for comparison. The prediction accuracy of all three models is evaluated on the testing data, and their performance is interpreted.

Finally, in Task 3, we delve into the theory behind regularized regression, exploring concepts like shrinkage and how LASSO and Ridge regression differ. This provides a deeper understanding of the strengths and trade-offs associated with these methods.

