This task involves applying regularized regression techniques to the Hitters dataset from the ISLR package, with Salary as the response variable. The data will be preprocessed to create a model matrix of predictors and split into training and testing sets in a 70:30 ratio. Using our custom LASSO implementation, we will determine the optimal regularization parameter (λ) and visualize the coefficient path. The results will be compared with the glmnet package. Additionally, Ridge regression and ordinary least squares (OLS) regression will be fitted, and predictions from all three models will be evaluated on the test set. Finally, we will interpret the performance of each model and analyze their strengths and limitations.

